</script>

In this code, we first set the side length of the outer square to 200 pixels, and the side length of each hole to 50 pixels. We then use the strokeRect method to draw strokes of 1 pixel width that form the wireframe of the outer square and each inner hole. The first two arguments of strokeRect represent the X and Y coordinates of the top-left corner of the rectangle, and the second two arguments represent the width and height of the rectangle.

By using strokeRect, we achieve a wireframe effect that consists of four squares, one inside the other, where the outer square and each inner square shares a common edge.
